---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service | Platform Usage & Licensing"
  description="Valtrix AI Terms of Service governing website usage, software evaluation, and enterprise testing studio licensing."
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 5rem;">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Terms of Service' }]} />

    <header class="section-hero" style="padding-top: 1rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; text-align: left;">
      <h1 class="heading-lg">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">Effective Date: November 2026 &bull; Valtrix AI</p>
    </header>

    <div class="card legal-content">
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing this website, evaluating Valtrix AI documentation, or engaging in technical pilots, you agree to comply with these terms, our security policies, and any applicable master services agreements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">2. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
        <p>
          All trademarks, logos, custom visual assets, and marketing content displayed on this website are the property of Valtrix AI. All rights in the underlying testing platform, architecture specifications, and software engines remain exclusively with the platform maintainers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">3. Software Evaluation &amp; Product Claims</h2>
        <p>
          Features and capabilities described on this marketing website reflect continuous development. Deployment performance, test execution speed, and concurrency capacities depend on customer infrastructure sizing, network topologies, and selected model architectures.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">4. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The website and promotional materials are provided on an "as-is" basis. Commercial software warranties and service level agreements (SLAs) are governed exclusively by formal enterprise subscription contracts.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
</style>

